OpenCADStudio-Termux patch 0003 -- save TEXT oblique angles in degrees.

This patch is different from 0001 and 0002: it does not touch the OpenCADStudio
checkout. It patches `opencadcodec`, which Cargo pulls as a git dependency into
its own checkout under $CARGO_HOME/git/checkouts/, so apply-patches.sh applies it
there after `cargo fetch` has downloaded the crate.

The bug
-------
DXF group 51 (TEXT oblique angle) is defined in degrees, but the entity stores
radians. The writer wrote the raw radian value, so a 15 degree slant was saved as
0.26. Reopening and saving again read that 0.26 as degrees and wrote 0.0046, so
the slant decayed toward zero on every save, silently and without any error.

Every other oblique write in the same file already converts with to_degrees():
STYLE group 50, ATTDEF group 51, ATTRIB group 51 and SHAPE group 51. TEXT was the
only one that did not.

Group 50 (STYLE) has its own regression test
(`text_style_oblique_angle_is_degrees_on_the_wire`). Group 51 had no test, which
is why this slipped through.

Verified: a drawing with 15 degrees of oblique comes back as 15 degrees after
three DXF save/reload cycles; the full opencadcodec test suite (58 suites) passes
with the change.

Upstream: HakanSeven12/opencadcodec, pinned at rev 42b44d2.

diff --git a/src/io/dxf/writer/section_writer.rs b/src/io/dxf/writer/section_writer.rs
index 259301a..a40be67 100644
--- a/src/io/dxf/writer/section_writer.rs
+++ b/src/io/dxf/writer/section_writer.rs
@@ -3868,7 +3868,11 @@ impl<'a, W: DxfStreamWriter> SectionWriter<'a, W> {
             self.writer.write_double(41, text.width_factor)?;
         }
         if text.oblique_angle != 0.0 {
-            self.writer.write_double(51, text.oblique_angle)?;
+            // Group 51 is degrees; the entity stores radians, exactly like
+            // STYLE's group 50. Written raw, every DXF save shrinks the
+            // angle toward zero: 15 deg becomes 0.26, then 0.0046.
+            self.writer
+                .write_double(51, text.oblique_angle.to_degrees())?;
         }
         self.writer.write_string(7, &text.style)?;
         if text.generation_flags != 0 {
